config SYSTEM_ENCFS
	bool "encfs: encrypted data volume control"
	default n
	depends on ENCFSMGR
	depends on BUILD_FLAT
	help
	  Control the encrypted data volume. Provision requires --erase.
	  With ENCFS_TESTING, testkey accepts a 32-byte hexadecimal test key,
	  restores the board key, or simulates a missing key provider. These
	  test commands require the volume to be stopped with no resources.
	  With ENCFS_KEYWRAP, rekey rotates the provider master identifier on
	  a mounted wrapped volume without replacing live data cipher keys.
	  Legacy directly-derived volumes reject rekey. With ENCFS_TESTING,
	  keyfiles selects the independent host-file simulator provider.
